Let $k>0$ and let $f_1,f_2$ be even $C^1$ functions on $\Sph$. If $f_1$ has zero projection onto $\mathcal H_2$, then  egin{equation} \mathcal B(f_1,f_2) \ge (\E f_1)(\E f_2) -c_{n,k}
orm{Qf_1}_2
orm{Qf_2}_2. \end{equation} The operator identity \eqref{eq:sign-operator} and this estimate also hold when $f_i=g_i^k$ for arbitrary norms $g_i$ on $\R^n$, with the vector fields defined almost everywhere. In that case  egin{equation} X_{g_i^k}(u)=g_i(u)^{k-1}
abla g_i(u). \end{equation}
